<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Harley-Davidson started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Harley-Davidson started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Mesirow Financial Inc said Tuesday it initiated coverage of Harley-Davidson Inc with a buy rating based on expected earnings growth resulting from &quot;tremendous demand.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Mesirow set an estimate for the Milwaukee-based company's earnings in 1997 of $2.24 a share, versus actual 1996 earnings of $1.90.</p>
<p>-- Mesirow cited Harley-Davidson's ability to charge a premium price for its motorcycles thanks to its &quot;visceral appeal,&quot; and the company's expanded production capacity expected by mid-1998.</p>
<p>-- Harley-Davidson is a leading motorcycle manufacturer.</p>
<p>-- Its shares were up 7/8 Tuesday at 37-3/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
